                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "This test seems to use `laststatus=3`. In that case it takes border characters from 'fillchars' options. Its `:h 'fillchars'` says the following about that particular separator: `vertright\t'├' or '|'\tright facing vertical separator`. I.e. its default can be either `├` or `|`. I am not entirely sure what conditions are for each to be used by default, but the there is the following note: \"If 'ambiwidth' is \"double\" then \"horiz\", \"horizup\", \"horizdown\", \"vert\", \"vertleft\", \"vertright\", \"verthoriz\", \"foldsep\" and \"fold\" default to single-byte alternatives.\"\r\n\r\nAs it passes locally and not on CI, I am fairly certain that this is not a 'mini.test' issue.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This test seems to use <code class=\"notranslate\">laststatus=3</code>. In that case it takes border characters from 'fillchars' options. Its <code class=\"notranslate\">:h 'fillchars'</code> says the following about that particular separator: <code class=\"notranslate\">vertright\t'├' or '|'\tright facing vertical separator</code>. I.e. its default can be either <code class=\"notranslate\">├</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code>. I am not entirely sure what conditions are for each to be used by default, but the there is the following note: \"If 'ambiwidth' is \"double\" then \"horiz\", \"horizup\", \"horizdown\", \"vert\", \"vertleft\", \"vertright\", \"verthoriz\", \"foldsep\" and \"fold\" default to single-byte alternatives.\"</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As it passes locally and not on CI, I am fairly certain that this is not a 'mini.test' issue.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "This test seems to use laststatus=3. In that case it takes border characters from 'fillchars' options. Its :h 'fillchars' says the following about that particular separator: vertright\t'├' or '|'\tright facing vertical separator. I.e. its default can be either ├ or |. I am not entirely sure what conditions are for each to be used by default, but the there is the following note: \"If 'ambiwidth' is \"double\" then \"horiz\", \"horizup\", \"horizdown\", \"vert\", \"vertleft\", \"vertright\", \"verthoriz\", \"foldsep\" and \"fold\" default to single-byte alternatives.\"\nAs it passes locally and not on CI, I am fairly certain that this is not a 'mini.test' issue.",
